From: Batman <noreply@batman.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bluez: generate the adapter IRK with getrandom(2) (#254 F26)

winson3QQ/Batman#254 stage 1 (PR-F). BlueZ generates the Identity Resolving Key through
bt_crypto_new(), which opens AF_ALG ecb(aes)/cmac(aes) sockets. The Batman kernel ships no
CRYPTO_USER_API (kmod-crypto-user is not in the image, on purpose: it would expose the kernel
crypto API to every local process), so no IRK was ever generated, set_privacy() never enabled
privacy and the node advertised with its public address (04, 1.5.12-wsl.3/.4: mgmt current
settings without "privacy"; "generate_and_write_irk() Failed to open crypto").
This adds feed patch 900 that takes the 16 bytes from getrandom(2) instead. Reading an existing
IRK never needed crypto. Design: docs/design/254-stage1-impl.md F26, §4.6.

Batman-Witness: file usr/bin/bluetoothd Generated IRK (getrandom)
--- /dev/null
+++ b/feeds/packages/utils/bluez/patches/900-batman-irk-getrandom.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+Batman #254 (F26): generate the adapter IRK with getrandom(2) instead of AF_ALG
+
+bt_crypto_new() opens AF_ALG ecb(aes)/cmac(aes) sockets; the Batman kernel ships no
+CRYPTO_USER_API, so the IRK was never generated and Privacy=device never took effect
+(04: current settings without 'privacy', public address on air).
+
+--- a/src/adapter.c
++++ b/src/adapter.c
+@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
+ #include <stdlib.h>
+ #include <stdbool.h>
+ #include <sys/ioctl.h>
++#include <sys/random.h>
+ #include <sys/file.h>
+ #include <sys/stat.h>
+ #include <dirent.h>
+@@ -4161,32 +4162,27 @@
+ static int generate_and_write_irk(uint8_t *irk, GKeyFile *key_file,
+ 							const char *filename)
+ {
+-	struct bt_crypto *crypto;
+ 	char str_irk_out[33];
+ 	gsize length = 0;
+ 	GError *gerr = NULL;
+ 	char *str;
+ 	int i;
+ 
+-	crypto = bt_crypto_new();
+-	if (!crypto) {
+-		error("Failed to open crypto");
++	/* Batman #254: take the 16 random bytes from getrandom(2), not from
++	 * bt_crypto_new(), which needs AF_ALG (ecb/cmac sockets) that this kernel
++	 * does not ship. Without an IRK set_privacy() never enables privacy and the
++	 * controller advertises with its public address. Blocks until the kernel
++	 * CRNG is ready; any failure leaves privacy off, as upstream does. */
++	if (getrandom(irk, 16, 0) != 16) {
++		error("Failed to generate IRK (getrandom): %s", strerror(errno));
+ 		return -1;
+ 	}
+ 
+-	if (!bt_crypto_random_bytes(crypto, irk, 16)) {
+-		error("Failed to generate IRK");
+-		bt_crypto_unref(crypto);
+-		return -1;
+-	}
+-
+-	bt_crypto_unref(crypto);
+-
+ 	for (i = 0; i < 16; i++)
+ 		sprintf(str_irk_out + (i * 2), "%02x", irk[i]);
+ 
+ 	str_irk_out[32] = '\0';
+-	info("Generated IRK successfully");
++	info("Generated IRK (getrandom)");
+ 
+ 	g_key_file_set_string(key_file, "General", "IdentityResolvingKey",
+ 								str_irk_out);
